            "body": "The gap is also hit without a kill, when several Nvim instances exit at once (here: a terminal app quitting with several windows open, each running Nvim). One whose `shada_write_file()` reaches the `os_fileinfo(fname, …)` check while another is between `os_remove(to)` and `os_rename()` finds no `main.shada`, fails with E137 and E136, and keeps its `main.shada.tmp.X`. I found three such leftovers, with timestamps matching servers that exited together.\n\nDeterministic repro with lldb (macOS, Nvim 0.12.4; `vim_rename()` is unchanged on master):\n\n```sh\nmkdir /tmp/race && cd /tmp/race\nnvim --headless -u NONE -i \"$PWD/main.shada\" +wshada +qa\n# B: stops once it has opened main.shada to merge it and created main.shada.tmp.a\nlldb -o 'b shada_write' -o run -- nvim -u NONE -i \"$PWD/main.shada\" --headless +qa\n# A, in another terminal in the same directory: stops in vim_rename(), after it deleted main.shada\nlldb -o 'b os_rename' -o run -- nvim -u NONE -i \"$PWD/main.shada\" --headless +qa\n# only main.shada.tmp.a and main.shada.tmp.b exist now; continue B, then A\n```\n\nB prints\n\n```\nE137: ShaDa file is not writable: /tmp/race/main.shada\nE136: Do not forget to remove /tmp/race/main.shada.tmp.a or rename it manually to /tmp/race/main.shada.\n```\n\nand `main.shada.tmp.a` stays.\n\nIn an `--embed` server whose UI has already gone, that error then blocks the exit forever (#42096): the three servers that left these files were still running a day or more later, in `getout()` → `wait_return()`.\n",
